.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt PQFREEBSD 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pqfreebsd
.Nd PQFreeBSD skeletal core kernel module
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the module at boot, place in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pqfreebsd_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Or at run time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload pqfreebsd
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the always-required
.Em pqk
core module for the
.Nm pqfreebsd
project
.Pq official name PQFreeBSD; evocative form Free(ly)B(le)S(se)D .
It holds suite
.Em enforcement
and
.Em audit
state and logs changes with
.Xr log 9 .
It does not implement feature policy and does not load sibling
.Nm pqfreebsd_*
modules; userland or
.Xr loader 8
loads those separately.
.Pp
Ideal steady state is
.Xr loader 8
preload.
.Xr kldload 8
is a same-session fallback until reboot.
Later ideal: full TPM e2e on that loader path
.Pq not this cut .
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are available under
.Va security.pqfreebsd :
.Bl -tag -width "enforcement"
.It Va enforcement
Suite enforcement switch
.Pq 0 off, 1 on; CTLFLAG_RWTUN .
A
.Xr log 9
.Dv LOG_NOTICE
message is emitted on change.
.It Va audit
Suite audit switch
.Pq 0 off, 1 on; CTLFLAG_RWTUN; same logging as
.Va enforcement .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr pqfreebsd_compat_zfs_multilabel 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr log 9
